  "question": {
    "text": "A stationary horizontal disc is free to rotate about its axis. When a torque is applied on it, its kinetic energy as a function of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math>, where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math> is the angle by which it has rotated, is given as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If its moment of inertia is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> then the angular acceleration of the disc is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>",
